  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $p(x)\\in \\mathbb{Q}[x]$. Is it true that $ A=\\{ p(n)+1/n : n\\in \\mathbb{N}\\} $ is strongly complete, in the sense that, for any finite set $B$, $ \\left\\{\\sum_{n\\in X}n : X\\subseteq A\\backslash B\\textrm{ finite }\\right\\} $ contains all sufficiently large integers?",
